  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "One ticket to a show costs \\(\\$20\\) at full price. Susan buys \\(4\\) tickets using a coupon that gives her a \\(25\\%\\) discount. Pam buys \\(5\\) tickets using a coupon that gives her a \\(30\\%\\) discount. How many more dollars does Pam pay than Susan?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(2\\)",
    "B": "\\(5\\)",
    "C": "\\(10\\)",
    "D": "\\(15\\)",
    "E": "\\(20\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "A \\(25\\%\\) discount means Susan pays \\(75\\%\\) of full price, while a \\(30\\%\\) discount means Pam pays \\(70\\%\\). Their total costs, in dollars, are\n\\[\n4\\cdot20\\cdot0.75=60,\n\\qquad\n5\\cdot20\\cdot0.70=70.\n\\]\nPam therefore pays \\(70-60=10\\) dollars more, choice \\(C\\).",
